    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21jZfxe5AmskoMP3AYBnVbr)_\n\nStacked on #48, which is stacked on #45. Merge in that order; GitHub retargets each PR as its base merges.\n\nBefore: the splash colours were two fixed greys chosen for dark or light backgrounds, plus the box face.\n\nAfter: a small framework of colour roles.\n- A role (`art`, `banner`, `footer`, `accent-1..3`) takes its colour from a face of the current theme (`shadow`, `font-lock-keyword-face`, ...) mixed towards the default background, so the lambda stays quiet and the accents stay vivid in any theme. `sp-splash-palette-roles` says which theme face, attribute and mix each role uses, so adding a role is one line.\n- `sp-splash-palettes` lets you choose colours for a particular theme by hand; roles not listed are still derived.\n- The menu boxes are coloured with the accent faces in turn (`sp-splash-accent-faces`), so each block has its own colour.\n- The splash is recoloured and redrawn when a theme is enabled or disabled (`enable-theme-functions`, `disable-theme-functions`; switch off with `sp-splash-palette-follow-theme`). `sp-splash-apply-palette` and `sp-splash-show-palette` do it and show it by hand.\n- `sp-splash.org` has a new \"Colour palette\" section and tangles to the same text as the `.el`; CHANGELOG entry added.\n\nChecked in headless Emacs 29.3 with faces set by hand: the roles came out as derived colours, a per-theme override won, the three boxes got the three accent faces, and enabling a test theme with a red `shadow` recoloured the art. Not checked: how the derived colours look on your real themes; tune the mix values in `sp-splash-palette-roles` if the art is too faint or too strong.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
